WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.347
In this video, you will learn how to run voting once it has started.

00:00:04.347 --> 00:00:09.496
You will pause and resume it, check the results, and remove a vote that should not count.

00:00:09.496 --> 00:00:10.640
We start on the map.

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:15.609
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.609 --> 00:00:17.734
That is the only address you need.

00:00:19.874 --> 00:00:22.281
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:26.025
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.362
Tap Use my location.

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:33.623
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:36.827
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:36.827 --> 00:00:41.388
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.649
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:48.844
See the three dots?

00:00:48.844 --> 00:00:53.147
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:53.685
Tap them.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.948
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:56.948 --> 00:01:02.286
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:01:04.015 --> 00:01:04.597
Tap Mine.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.228
This is your personal page.

00:01:06.228 --> 00:01:11.588
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.318
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:18.989
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:20.897 --> 00:01:24.678
This card is where you control the contest while it is running.

00:01:24.678 --> 00:01:27.573
Voting opens and closes on your dates by itself.

00:01:27.573 --> 00:01:30.646
The Controls card lets you step in when you need to.

00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:35.034
Say you spot something odd, or you need to fix a mistake.

00:01:35.034 --> 00:01:39.184
Tap Pause voting, and votes stop right away, until you say otherwise.

00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:44.451
When you are ready, tap Resume voting, and voting carries on.

00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:47.267
Now tap Results.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.995
Here is the full tally, category by category.

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:57.053
You can always see the counts, even when you have hidden them from the public so people are not swayed by who is ahead.

00:01:58.879 --> 00:02:00.765
Open Review individual votes.

00:02:00.765 --> 00:02:04.033
Every single vote is listed, with when it was cast.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:10.570
The system flags odd patterns, like a burst of votes within a few seconds, so you can look more closely.

00:02:12.392 --> 00:02:15.320
If a vote should not count, tap Void next to it.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.340
It is removed from the tally, and you can restore it later if you change your mind.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.013
This keeps the contest fair.

00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:26.585
Next up: Add co-organizers and judges.
